Build a complete, production-quality responsive web application called:

# Education Sales Counselling Training

This is a simple internal training and assessment platform for education counsellors.

The application must be intentionally SIMPLE.

Do NOT turn this into a complex LMS.

The core user journey is:

ENTER NAME → TRAINING DASHBOARD → 11 CHAPTERS → WATCH VIDEOS → TAKE INDIVIDUAL CHAPTER ASSESSMENTS → FINAL ASSESSMENT → RESULT → GENERATE/DOWNLOAD PDF ASSESSMENT REPORT.

The user does NOT need to create an account.

The user does NOT need a password.

The user does NOT need OTP authentication.

The user simply enters their name and starts.

==================================================
1. CORE REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

The application must support:

1. User manually enters their name.
2. Anyone can enter any name and use the platform.
3. Generate a hidden unique local user/session ID for each new training record.
4. Remember the user's training state persistently.
5. State must survive:
   - page refresh
   - browser restart
   - accidental tab closure
   - navigating away and returning
   - temporary internet loss
   - logout
6. Logout must NOT delete the user's saved training data.
7. If the same user later enters the same name on the same browser/device, allow the application to recover the existing saved training record.
8. Do NOT build passwords, OTPs, email authentication or account registration.
9. Do NOT build an admin dashboard in V1.
10. Do NOT build complicated analytics.
11. Do NOT build gamification.
12. Do NOT build chapter locking.
13. Do NOT require 80%/90% video completion before assessment.
14. Do NOT force users to complete chapters sequentially.
15. Every chapter should be accessible at any time.
16. Every chapter has its own video and its own assessment.
17. There is one final assessment for the complete course.
18. At the end, generate an Assessment Report.
19. The user can download the PDF report multiple times.
20. The report data must remain saved until the user chooses to reset/delete the local training record.

