3. PERSISTENCE / AUTOSAVE
==================================================

This is a CRITICAL requirement.

Do not rely only on React state.

All important state must be persisted using browser persistent storage.

For V1, use localStorage for the main state.

If a larger storage mechanism is genuinely required, IndexedDB may be used, but keep the implementation simple.

The application must automatically save:

- user name
- user ID
- current chapter
- last opened chapter
- video playback position for each chapter
- chapter assessment answers
- chapter assessment attempts
- chapter assessment scores
- chapter assessment best scores
- chapter assessment completion status
- final assessment answers
- final assessment current question
- final assessment attempts
- final assessment scores
- final assessment completion
- final report data
- report generated status
- timestamps

Every important interaction should autosave immediately.

For example:

When a user selects an answer:
SAVE.

When a user changes question:
SAVE.

When the video playback position changes:
SAVE periodically.

When an assessment starts:
SAVE.

When an assessment is submitted:
SAVE.

When the final report is generated:
SAVE.

Never allow a refresh to erase assessment answers.

